[White "5.3 Centralization"]
[Black "Centralization"]
[Result "*"]

 { Another key idea in endgames with queens on the board is centralization. Queens, in contrast to rooks, control more squares the more centrally placed they are, and the fact that usually only one queen can occupy the centre at a time makes the latter a treasured area. We saw proof of this idea in Polugaevsky-Tal; here are some more examples. }  
 *

