 { Thanks to his more active queen and the chronic weakness on d4, Black is a bit better. His first priority is to improve the queen. } 1... { -KEY- } Qf5+ 2. Kc1 Qd5 $1 { The weak d4-pawn is already starting to make itself felt. } 3. Qf2 f5 { The next step in Black's plan is to open a new front on the kingside by ...h6-h5-h4 and ...Kh7-g6-h5 - Gershon. } 4. Kc2 Qc4+ 5. Kd2 Qb3 6. Kc1 Qd3 { Korchnoi adjusts his plans slightly and regroups the queen to e4. } 7. Qd2 Qe4 $1 { Here and later, Black has no reason to swap his active queen. } 8. b3 Kg7 { Resuming the plan indicated in the third note. } 9. a4 Kg6 10. Qd1 ( { After } 10. Kb2 h5 { it is not clear what should White do next. } ) 
Qe3+ 11. Kc2 h5 12. Qd3 ( { Obviously, } 12. d5 $2 { failed to } Qc5 ) 
Qf2+ ( { The queens are needed on the board in order to keep White's king away. Instead after } 12... Qxd3 $2 13. Kxd3 h4 14. Ke3 Kh5 15. Kf3 { followed by h2-h3 Black would not be able to progress. } ) 
13. Qd2 Qg1 14. Kb2 h4 $1 { Finally, Black's play takes concrete shape. } 15. gxh4 Kh5 16. d5 $1 { Seeing that he is being left with weak pawns on the kingside, Hernandez looks for counterplay on the rest of the board. } exd5 17. Qxd5 Qxh2+ 18. Ka3 Qxf4 19. Qxb7 ( 19. Qxf7 Kxh4 20. Qxb7 { was preferable - Hecht, when Black could consider } Qd6 21. Ka2 Qd2 22. Ka3 f4 { keeping some chances for a win. } ) 
Qd6+ 20. Ka2 Qd2+ 21. Ka3 Qc1+ 22. Kb4 $6 { This just helps the black queen to find a better square on e6; } ( { so } 22. Ka2 { was preferable - Hecht. } ) 
Qe1+ 23. Kb5 ( { In the event of } 23. Ka3 Qa1 24. Kb4 Qd4 $1 { Black manages to centralize his queen, with definite winning chances after } 25. Ka3 f4 26. Qxf7 Kxh4 ) 
Qe6 $1 24. b4 $6 ( { a) Or } 24. Qxa7 Qxb3 25. Ka5 f4 { with similar play to the previous note } ) 
 ( { b) But } 24. Qf3 { first was a better move order; e.g. } Kxh4 25. Qf4 Kh5 26. b4 { with more resistance than in the game. } ) 
f4 $1 { Betting on the passed pawn. } 25. Qf3+ ( { After } 25. Qxa7 f3 26. Qa8 Qe2 27. Kb6 f2 { Black wins by using the enemy h-pawn as a shield; e. g. } 28. Qh8 Kg4 29. Qg7 Kh3 30. Qc3 Kh2 31. Qc7 Kg2 32. Qc6 Qf3 33. Qc2 Kh1 { - Gershon. } ) 
Qg4 { This resource would not have been possible had White played 24.Qf3+ first. } 26. Qd5+ Kxh4 27. Qh1+ Kg5 28. Qc1 Qd7+ ( { In view of } 28... Qd7 29. Ka5 ( { or } 28... Qd7+ 28. Ka6 Qxa4 30. Kb7 Qxb4 ) 
Qd8 30. Kb5 Qb6 31. Kc4 Qc6 { - Hecht, White resigned. } ) 

 0-1

